 ## Overview
-This method reduces the memory footprint of a chunk-based mesh by removing unreferenced vertices and renumbering the remaining ones to form a dense, contiguous array. It solves the problem of sparse vertex buffers that arise during incremental blocky meshing, where vertices are allocated per voxel face but many are culled or unused. Unlike [Voxel Face Meshing with Packed Attributes](4153-voxel-face-meshing-with-packed-attributes.md), which focuses on storage layout, this method actively compacts the data. It differs from [Chunk Mesh Data Structure & Buffer Update](4182-chunk-mesh-data-structure-buffer-update.md) by performing the logical remapping rather than just updating buffer pointers.
+This method compacts vertex buffers by removing unreferenced vertices and renumbering the remaining ones into a dense, contiguous array [S1, unofficial]. It addresses sparse vertex buffers generated during incremental blocky meshing, where vertices are allocated per voxel face but many are culled or unused [G]. Unlike [Voxel Face Meshing with Packed Attributes](4153-voxel-face-meshing-with-packed-attributes.md), which optimizes storage layout, this method actively reduces vertex count [G]. It differs from [Chunk Mesh Data Structure & Buffer Update](4182-chunk-mesh-data-structure-buffer-update.md) by performing logical remapping of indices and data rather than merely updating buffer pointers [G].
 
